This directory contains versioned MySQL schema migrations.

Run from backend/:
  python -m alembic upgrade head
  python -m alembic current
  python -m alembic upgrade head --sql > sql/001_initial_schema.sql

Offline SQL generation requires no database credentials or network connection.
Online migrations read .env.mysql and environment overrides. They require a
dedicated EMPTY database for the initial revision. No MongoDB data import or
application cutover occurs merely by running Alembic. The separate Step 2
importer and application use the migrated schema. Never run downgrade against production
data: MySQL DDL is not a transactionally reversible data backup.

The initial revision is an immutable snapshot. It does NOT call create_all()
on current application models. Shared MySQL 5.7 compilation policies apply
DYNAMIC row format, omit unsupported native CHECK syntax and adapt the known
legacy point_logs.note TEXT default. Tests compare the frozen revision's
rendered schema to the reviewed full SQL export and current relational model.
